    {
      "id": "ee2de39d-6da3-4299-9b71-0f0b7a2473a8",
      "name": "Sticky Note 65841e1a",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1232,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 1056,
        "content": "## Flag high-engagement comments and open questions on YouTube videos\n\n**Who's it for:** channel owners and community managers who want to reply to what matters instead of scrolling hundreds of comments per video by hand.\n\n**What it does:** monitors a watchlist of YouTube videos, fetches new comments via the Apify YouTube Comments Downloader actor, then triages them instead of dumping a flat list: fetch failures (comments disabled, video unavailable) get flagged, comments with 10+ likes get flagged as worth a reply, genuine questions get flagged too - everything else (the bulk of ordinary comments) is silently dropped on purpose, since a triage tool should surface only what needs attention.\n\nEvery run also logs one audit row (fetch failures, flagged comments, watchlist health changes) to a run_log tab, and a separate monthly flow excludes videos that have been failing to fetch for 7+ straight days from the daily read (saving API spend), giving each one exactly one fresh retry a month in case it gets fixed.\n\n**Requirements:** an Apify account (pay-per-comment, no subscription, and the free account gives you $5/month of platform credit to start) and a Google account for Sheets access. This template uses the community node @apify/n8n-nodes-apify - install it from the nodes panel (search \"Apify\") before running. Verified and Cloud-installable, works self-hosted too.\n\n**How to set up:**\n1. Install the Apify community node if not already.\n2. Make a copy of the template sheet (watchlist + flagged_comments + run_log tabs), paste your own video URLs into the watchlist tab.\n3. Replace the sheet references in this workflow with your copy's ID.\n4. Attach your own Google Sheets and Apify credentials.\n5. Swap the manual trigger for a Schedule Trigger to monitor on a cadence (e.g. daily), and leave the monthly maintenance schedule trigger as-is (or adjust its cadence).\n\n**How to customize:** adjust the like-count and question-detection thresholds on the triage switch node, and the 7-day/30-day windows on the maintenance filters, to match your channel.\n\nCost: charged per comment returned by the actor (maxCommentsPerVideo caps this per video), nothing extra for the triage or health-tracking logic."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9e57610c-ce98-455b-93ec-6c1c6ab06ca0",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3eb0561d",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1456,
        -128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 576,
        "height": 224,
        "content": "**Why triage, not a dump**\nA plain comment scraper returns every comment as one flat list - hundreds of rows per video, most of them irrelevant. This workflow only surfaces the ones worth a human's time: fetch failures, high-engagement comments, and open questions. Everything else is silently dropped."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1fdd228c-c134-48dc-a40a-5238389a463d",
      "name": "Prerequisites",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -528,
        384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 556,
        "height": 288,
        "content": "## What you'll need\n- A free Apify account (console.apify.com) - pay per comment returned, no subscription, and the free account gives you $5/month of platform credit to start\n- A Google account for Sheets access via OAuth\n- A list of YouTube video URLs you want to keep an eye on\n\n**New here?** Every node has a note in its right-hand panel explaining what it does and why - click any node once to read it before you change anything."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f117e96c-1569-47ac-bbd9-f28f35e39ead",
      "name": "Summarize video health",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "notes": "One outcome per unique video this run: any success:false item makes it 'failing', otherwise 'healthy'. Feeds the watchlist health tracker below, independent of the comment-level triage above.",
      "position": [
        768,
        512
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const rows = $input.all();\nconst byVideo = {};\nfor (const item of rows) {\n  const j = item.json;\n  const url = j.videoUrl;\n  if (!url) continue;\n  if (!byVideo[url]) byVideo[url] = { hasSuccess: false, hasFailure: false };\n  if (j.success === false) byVideo[url].hasFailure = true;\n  if (j.success === true) byVideo[url].hasSuccess = true;\n}\nconst now = new Date().toISOString();\nreturn Object.entries(byVideo).map(([video_url, v]) => ({\n  json: {\n    video_url,\n    outcome: v.hasFailure ? 'failing' : 'healthy',\n    last_failed_at: v.hasFailure ? now : '',\n  },\n}));"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
