    {
      "id": "f61c38b8-f4d9-43a1-b9ae-ce31f129e9fc",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Health tracking",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        784
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 416,
        "content": "**Why this needs two systems, not one**\nA digest workflow like this re-checks every video on every run - there's no per-row \"done\" state to get stuck on the way the enrichment templates have. But a video CAN get permanently broken (comments disabled, video deleted, taken private), and without tracking that, you'd keep paying for a fetch that will never succeed.\n\nSo this workflow tracks fetch health on the watchlist itself, separately from the flagged_comments output: a failure sets status=failing and stamps last_failed_at; a success clears it. Once a video has been failing for 7+ straight days, the monthly maintenance flow (bottom-left) escalates it to chronically_failing, which excludes it from the daily read entirely - and gives it exactly one fresh retry a month, so a fixed video isn't excluded forever."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
